      "license": "MIT",
      "testOnly": true,
      "homepage": "https://github.com/tafia/quick-xml",
      "rationale": "🩹️ RECLASSIFIED (ticket SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION, shard A10, 2026-09-02). This entry was registered `third-party-library` on the strength of a real crate that does genuine codec work, but the mutation's expected RESULT is computed by this owner's own `./🦀️.rs` -- its dispatch function's catch-all arm is `\"mutation kind {...} has no oracle implementation\"`, proof that every OTHER arm is an implementation, not a reading. Both halves of the comparison then descend from the same specification, so a shared misreading produces two agreeing wrong answers -- the one failure a differential oracle exists to catch. This is a `cross-semio-implementation`: a required SUPPLEMENT (metamorphic/inverse/round-trip evidence), never a substitute. A qualifying third-party reference for the mutation semantics is still owed. See $TICKET/📓️a10-oracle-honesty.md.\n\nquick-xml is a general streaming XML reader AND writer, not a validating processor: it hands the DOCTYPE back as one raw string and never looks at it again, which is exactly what makes it usable as the independent producer for a VALIDITY vocabulary. This subset's oracle (./🦀️.rs) builds its document tree from quick-xml's event stream through the shared 📰markup family module, then decomposes that raw DOCTYPE with its OWN hand-rolled XML 1.0 §2.8/§4.2 grammar, applies each declared XmlValidMutation kind, derives the four §2.8/§2.9 verdicts straight from the W3C text, and re-serializes with quick-xml's Writer. It never imports this repository's own parse_doctype/xml_document_to_text codec, nor its check_valid_conformance. Both encode the same normative rules; neither is derived from the other, which is the point. Registered by this subset rather than shared with ✳️any because the two catalogs have exactly one kind in common (set-text) and disagree about what the DOCTYPE is for.",
      "hostPath": "✏️s/🔌️plugins/🗄️stdio/🧪️oracle/📦️packages/🦀️rust",
      "kind": "cross-semio-implementation",
